The formula used for calculating the therapeutic index is expressed as follows:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${{\mathrm{Therapeutic}}}\,{{\mathrm{index}}}=\frac{{{\mathrm{IC}}}50\,{{\mathrm{in}}}\,{{\mathrm{NHA}}}}{{{\mathrm{IC}}}50\,{{\mathrm{inindividual}}}\,{{\mathrm{tumor}}}\,{{\mathrm{cell}}}\,{{\mathrm{line}}}}$$\end{document}Therapeuticindex=IC50inNHAIC50inindividualtumorcelllineWhere:
IC50 in NHA represents the half-maximal inhibitory concentration of GB13 in primary cells of the central nervous system (CNS).
IC50 in individual tumor cell line represents the half-maximal inhibitory concentration of GB13 in the specific HGG cell line under consideration.
